Page https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/transports.md

  The page defines the HTTP wire behavior in prose and holds no
  JSON-RPC example messages, so it has no fixture files. The norms its
  text fixes, which the HTTP transport tests pin: every client message
  is a POST to one endpoint; Accept lists both application/json and
  text/event-stream; a notification or response POST is answered 202
  with no body; a request POST is answered with Content-Type
  application/json (one JSON object) or text/event-stream (the
  response may follow other messages on the stream); the client
  includes MCP-Session-Id on every request after initialize, echoing
  the value initialize returned; the client includes
  MCP-Protocol-Version on HTTP requests. Fetched 2026-11-18.

